.TH QCLI 1 "July 2026" "qcli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qcli \- one query shell for cloud data platforms
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qcli
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB--target\fR \fITARGET\fR]
.br
.B qcli
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
qcli executes native SQL against configured Trino, Databricks SQL, and
Snowflake targets. Interactive, batch, and HTTP frontends share one session and
query execution core.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config path|check|show
Inspect and validate configuration.
.TP
.B target list|show|test|capabilities
Inspect targets and test connectivity.
.TP
.B auth key create ID
Generate an opaque HTTP API key and Argon2id hash.
.TP
.B serve
Start the HTTP service. See \fBqcli --help\fR for production options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.qcli/.env
Default sectioned target configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.qcli/http-auth.toml
Suggested HTTP caller authentication configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
The qcli README and milestone documentation distributed with the source.
